WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:08.150
Gold Roger, the legendary King of the Pirates, obtained everything the world has to offer.

3
00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:12.890
What he said in his final moments drove countless souls to the seas.

4
00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:17.430
You want my treasure? Go ahead. Find it!

5
00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.830
Everything is right where I left it!

6
00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.840
Pirates have set out in pursuit of their dreams!

7
00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:25.440
The world has truly entered... the Great Pirate Era!

8
00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:29.380
Gotta keep movin’, just can't stop

9
00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:33.780
Rarin’ for the dawn to arrive

10
00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:37.480
One, two, sunshine, four, we go!

11
00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:43.290
Hoist the flag for the break of romance dawn

12
00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:49.500
Jump-start your day, ready to make waves

13
00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:54.200
Reachin’ for fantastic realms

14
00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:58.370
Need to put your toughness on display

15
00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:01.680
Is bein’ brazen such a crime?

16
00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:04.480
If you’re wanted, you’re a winner

17
00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:09.620
Ah, freedom is our only rule

18
00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:15.660
Worries don’t bother us at all

19
00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:18.430
Keep on goin’, that's our pledge

20
00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:22.030
Since the day our dreams began

21
00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:26.870
Our aims remain the same

22
00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:29.240
Sunlight won’t fade from our hearts

23
00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:33.670
The sun of my heart will never set

24
00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:40.450
One, two, sunshine... One, two, sunshine

25
00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:47.850
One, two, sunshine, four, we go!

26
00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:51.930
We go!

27
00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:59.840
<b>10,000 Meters Under the Sea</b>

28
00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:56.270
An undersea volcano...
 Straight ahead!

29
00:01:56.830 --> 00:01:58.300
Looks like it's about to blow!

30
00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:02.510
Pull back, men!

31
00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:04.710
We'll live to plunder another day!

32
00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:06.520
– Yeah!
– Yeah, Roger!

33
00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.680
You don't gotta ask me twice!

34
00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:11.720
Ankoro! Wadatsumi! Draw the ship!

35
00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:13.120
Okay, Captain, sure!

36
00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:18.020
Vander Decken is my name,
and these long-lost riches I'll get later!

37
00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:18.020
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

38
00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.130
Oh, no!

39
00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:23.560
Luffy, I don't know 
how the Kraken works,

40
00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:26.330
but order him to turn
 around and haul ass!

41
00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:29.000
Hey, Surume!

42
00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.170
Wait a sec...

43
00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.910
He's hauling ass just fine all on his own.

44
00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:37.440
For such a giant monster,
it's kind of shameful, actually.

45
00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:39.780
Who cares? I would be doing the same thing!

46
00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:44.210
He runs terribly.

47
00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:45.820
Give him a break!

48
00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:48.790
I'd rather be clumsy and
alive than graceful and dead!

49
00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:50.790
Like... me?

50
00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:52.890
What the hell is mouth brow doing?

51
00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:56.360
Whoo! Yeah! Baby!

52
00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:57.560
It's rehab!

53
00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:02.530
Come on! I wanna see lava!

54
00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:04.870
Evacuate to the front of the ship!

55
00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:05.940
Hurry!

56
00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:09.210
That's not gonna help!
It's just a couple of feet!

57
00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:29.030
Well, you got your lava, Luffy.

58
00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:31.460
It's getting hotter.

59
00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:34.260
Nobody told me we could
be boiled alive down here!

60
00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:35.470
Hot! Hot!

61
00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:36.370
The ocean sure hates us!

62
00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:48.850
Their ship's flying. Is that good or bad?

63
00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:54.350
Faster, Surume!

64
00:03:54.350 --> 00:03:56.020
You can do it!

65
00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:58.270
If you don't hurry it up,
somebody is gonna be eating

66
00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:01.290
your delicious cooked carcass
from off the ocean floor!

67
00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:07.430
Riding him is pretty fun,
but eating him might be even better!

68
00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:13.540
The temperature change–
it's causing a vortex in the current!

69
00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.150
Nami,

70
00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:18.480
which direction is Fishman Island?
We can't lose our wa–

71
00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:21.040
You're not ready for real girls yet, Sanji!

72
00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:23.080
Go back to your pictures and relax!

73
00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:25.950
Straight ahead. I have an idea!

74
00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:29.120
We're getting closer!

75
00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:34.530
Now, jump into the trench!

76
00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:44.170
That doesn't look safe!

77
00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:48.810
That's not a place you jump! It's an abyss!

78
00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:51.980
Yeah, there's nothing but
blackness down there!

79
00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:55.650
Fish people live there?
 They've gotta be insane!

80
00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:04.050
Lava! There's lava behind us!

81
00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:06.760
And the void in front of us! Help!

82
00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:09.490
Can't we go up?
Up, where it's not burning and dark

83
00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:12.030
and everything wants to kill us?

84
00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:14.340
Wait! You're not really Luffy, are you?

85
00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:17.030
You're some evil demon who looks
 like him that wants to drag us

86
00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:18.870
to the depths of hell!

87
00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:21.240
This is a nightmare! Why
can't I wake up? Why?

88
00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:23.470
Surume! Jump in!

89
00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:32.720
It's erupting again!

90
00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:36.850
Whoa, look above us!

91
00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:38.460
Something's coming down!

92
00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:40.160
Boulders?

93
00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:41.120
A mudslide?

94
00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:43.060
It's an avalanche! Brace yourselves!

95
00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:45.530
The eruption knocked the rocks loose!

96
00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:47.860
Dodge the boulders, Surume!

97
00:05:51.070 --> 00:05:52.900
I can't just sit here; I'm gonna go cut 'em!

98
00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:55.870
Luffy, hold onto my leg, okay?

99
00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:57.070
Sure! Gotcha!

100
00:05:58.110 --> 00:05:59.480
Zoro! You can't!

101
00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:01.910
What's the big idea?

102
00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:04.510
The ship is over 8,000 meters deep right now!

103
00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:06.050
Never mind the boulders!

104
00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:07.950
Go outside and the water
 pressure will crush you!

105
00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:09.990
Fine, but we gotta do something!

106
00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:11.960
Leave it to me, then!

107
00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:14.260
Special Attack, Green Star...

108
00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:15.990
Sargasso!

109
00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:23.600
Usopp made seaweed appear!

110
00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:25.840
Oh, wow! Nice shot!

111
00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:28.210
It won't hold for very long, though.

112
00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:30.310
We gotta get moving, Surume! Move it!

113
00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:41.120
Just in time!

114
00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:49.460
Monster plants? Aw man! That's cool!

115
00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:52.160
I wonder what else you
have in that bag of tricks!
Yes, I know I'm awesome.
Praise me more!

116
00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:54.130
Looks like we're in the clear!

117
00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:59.140
You were pretty great, too, Surume!
Thanks a bunch!

118
00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:00.600
Yeah! You saved us all!

119
00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.110
You're the best, Surume!

120
00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:09.850
– Surume! Yay!
– Surume! Yay!

121
00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:10.350
– Suru–
– Suru–

122
00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:35.870
<b>10,000 Meters Below Sea Level
The Deep (The Bottom of the Oceanic Trench)</b>

123
00:07:36.210 --> 00:07:38.740
Are we alive? Or dead?

124
00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:40.510
There's light,

125
00:07:40.510 --> 00:07:42.550
but we're so deep in the sea.

126
00:07:42.550 --> 00:07:45.450
So bright! I've got stars in my eyes!

127
00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:49.750
Rather, just stars. There aren't any eyes.
Nya, ho, ho, ho...

128
00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:52.420
Guys! Check it out!

129
00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:54.730
Over there! I think we made it!

130
00:07:55.590 --> 00:07:57.730
I can't see anything. It's too bright.

131
00:07:57.730 --> 00:07:59.430
C'mon, Nami. Tell us!

132
00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:02.070
Yep! There's no doubt about it!

133
00:08:02.070 --> 00:08:04.330
The needle is pointing straight ahead.

134
00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:05.440
We did it.

135
00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:09.310
Fishman Island!

136
00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:11.410
It's huge!

137
00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:14.210
It's in a giant bubble!

138
00:08:14.210 --> 00:08:16.150
It looks like they have clouds!

139
00:08:16.150 --> 00:08:18.150
There must be air inside.

140
00:08:21.740 --> 00:08:24.020
All right!

141
00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.620
We made it!

142
00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:29.290
The New World is next! Almost there!

143
00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:33.100
Well, what do ya know.
The morons survived after all!

144
00:08:35.630 --> 00:08:38.000
This is where the mermaids live.

145
00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:39.800
Real-life, beautiful mermaids!

146
00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:42.170
My dream can finally come true.

147
00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:46.480
– Yeah! Yeah! Yeah! Yeah! – Whoa! Yeah!

148
00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:46.480
How I've longed to see
their faces. To touch them!

149
00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:50.610
– ♪ A mermaid for me! ♪
– ♪ A mermaid for me! ♪

150
00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:53.020
– ♪ A mermaid for you! ♪
– ♪ A mermaid for you! ♪

151
00:08:53.020 --> 00:08:55.050
– ♪ A mermaid for– ♪
– ♪ A mermaid for– ♪

152
00:08:55.050 --> 00:08:58.660
Hold up! You're not ready for this!
You shouldn't even think about it!

153
00:08:58.660 --> 00:08:59.520
Sanji!

154
00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:10.830
I'm sorry!

155
00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:12.900
I thought my treatment would do the trick!

156
00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:16.140
I know it's your dream,
but you're not healthy enough for mermaids.

157
00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:17.640
Doctor!

158
00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:22.010
For him, this is a fate worse than death.
There's gotta be something you can do!

159
00:09:22.010 --> 00:09:24.510
If he sees mermaids, it will be death!

160
00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:25.480
How cruel.

161
00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:29.090
I don't care...

162
00:09:29.090 --> 00:09:29.890
Sanji!

163
00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:34.620
I-I don't wanna live in
 a world without dreams...

164
00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:38.360
I'd rather die leering at some hot mermaid tail.

165
00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:39.800
You're the worst!

166
00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:44.840
Who needs blood?
 I have lust to sustain me!

167
00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:45.700
Whoa!

168
00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:47.040
His lechery burns bright!

169
00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:50.140
I'm so hungry!

170
00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:53.980
I bet they fry up all kinds of yummy
deep-sea monsters down here!

171
00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:56.280
Hey, wipe up that drool

172
00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:57.850
and tell Surume to go.

173
00:09:57.850 --> 00:10:00.650
There's an entrance around here
somewhere, and we've gotta find it.

174
00:10:00.650 --> 00:10:02.350
Guys! We got company!

175
00:10:05.090 --> 00:10:10.230
Why would you allow these foolish humans
to tell you what to do, Kraken?

176
00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:14.000
Well, crap. That's not good.

177
00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:16.900
Sea monsters! Giant ones!

178
00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:21.570
So close! And now we're dead!

179
00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:26.540
Wow, they look tough! I want one!

180
00:10:28.180 --> 00:10:30.580
Wait, is somebody riding 'em?

181
00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:38.520
What the heck, Surume?

182
00:10:38.520 --> 00:10:41.020
Seriously, we were almost there!

183
00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:58.170
Whoa, it's like a whole circus of sea monsters!

184
00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:02.410
You guys are the Straw
Hat Pirates, aren't you?

185
00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:06.280
You have quite the reputation.

186
00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:11.760
For starters, you were the ones
who ruined the Arlong Pirates' plans.

187
00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:16.860
That part makes sense at least.

188
00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:19.600
But for some reason,
 two years back,

189
00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:22.400
when Hachi was in trouble,
you stood up for your old enemy.

190
00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:27.600
And then, you clocked one of the
Celestial Dragons right in his ugly face.

191
00:11:29.110 --> 00:11:35.310
Fisher Tiger happened to do the exact same
thing, and he's the hero of this entire island.

192
00:11:35.950 --> 00:11:37.810
Fisher... Tiger...?

193
00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:42.790
<b>Fighter Hammond
New Fishman Pirates</b>

194
00:11:40.250 --> 00:11:42.790
I'm not sure what to do with you.

195
00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:44.390
Tell it to me straight.

196
00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:48.530
<b>Assassin Hyozo
New Fishman Pirates</b>

197
00:11:44.390 --> 00:11:47.190
Are you supposed to be our enemies or not?

198
00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:54.830
<b>Fighter Kasagon
New Fishman Pirates</b>

199
00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:51.660
How about I give you an option?

200
00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:55.970
Enlist under our banner as members
of the New Fishman Pirates, or else!

201
00:11:56.670 --> 00:11:57.300
“Or else”

202
00:11:57.300 --> 00:12:01.370
meaning we sink you right now.

203
00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:02.670
What'd you say?

204
00:12:03.670 --> 00:12:05.710
Fuel up, Franky! Hurry!

205
00:12:05.710 --> 00:12:07.310
Huh? You got a plan?

206
00:12:07.710 --> 00:12:11.280
You and I both know that Luffy
isn't gonna cooperate with these guys.

207
00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:15.620
But we're 10,000 meters underwater
right now, and if we try to fight them,

208
00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:18.990
we don't stand a chance of winning,
especially not with those sea monsters.

209
00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:20.520
So, we have to go!

210
00:12:20.520 --> 00:12:22.920
I need you to use all of the oxygen we have

211
00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:26.030
to make a giant Coup de Burst
so we can charge straight into Fishman Island!

212
00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:28.800
Whoa, are you kiddin' me?

213
00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:32.400
We've come way too far to die here.

214
00:12:33.340 --> 00:12:37.840
I agree. It's risky, but it's likely
 our only chance at surviving this.

215
00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:40.610
If that's the case, I'm
gonna fill it up right away!

216
00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:42.380
Franky, steer the ship!

217
00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:44.750
Everything's gonna be just super!

218
00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:52.120
So, have you decided if you want
to be part of our crew, Straw Hat Luffy?

219
00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:55.160
Yeah, right. You wish!

220
00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:56.630
Stupid!

221
00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:01.630
Are you sure about that?

222
00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:05.540
You did hear me say what will
happen if you refuse, didn't you?

223
00:13:05.940 --> 00:13:08.510
Guess you are the enemy of the Fishmen!

224
00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:11.040
Nothing but filthy human scum!

225
00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:18.450
Why would I wanna work
for a big dumb fish face like you?

226
00:13:18.450 --> 00:13:20.050
Cut it out, Luffy. You'll make him mad!

227
00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:22.250
That's a real shame.

228
00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:25.190
You won't be seeing Fishman Island after all.

229
00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:28.160
Get ready to sink, Straw Hats!

230
00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:30.160
Sea Lion!

231
00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:36.700
All right, filled up and ready to move!

232
00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:38.330
Franky! You're up!

233
00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:40.770
Take them down!

234
00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:42.340
Bring it on!

235
00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:46.810
Franky, let's go!

236
00:13:47.140 --> 00:13:49.110
Hey, don't forget, we got our own lion!

237
00:13:50.610 --> 00:13:53.250
Maybe we can fight some other time, all right?

238
00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:55.090
Here it goes.

239
00:13:55.090 --> 00:13:58.050
Coup de Burst!

240
00:14:03.260 --> 00:14:04.230
Look at 'em go!

241
00:14:13.670 --> 00:14:15.970
Can't breathe. There's no more air.

242
00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:19.340
We're getting squished.

243
00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:22.650
It's hard to breathe,

244
00:14:22.650 --> 00:14:25.250
and that's not just because I don't have lungs.

245
00:14:26.450 --> 00:14:29.420
Hang on! We'll make it, no matter what!

246
00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:36.030
What in the hell?!
What's up with that crazy ship?!

247
00:14:36.030 --> 00:14:38.230
We're on our way in!

248
00:14:38.030 --> 00:14:40.730
I'll be with you soon, beautiful mermaids!

249
00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:50.740
We lost the coating!

250
00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:54.280
It got stuck when we crossed the bubble!

251
00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:57.280
Look up there!

252
00:14:58.110 --> 00:14:59.680
What could it be?

253
00:15:00.680 --> 00:15:03.850
This bubble. It's a double structure!

254
00:15:04.150 --> 00:15:07.360
A normal ship would crash
because there's nothing but air!

255
00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:10.660
We're about to run into another bubble!

256
00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:12.130
You guys ready?

257
00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:21.470
Water?

258
00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:36.050
This current is really strong!

259
00:15:40.760 --> 00:15:42.760
Help... me...

260
00:15:42.760 --> 00:15:44.490
Can't breathe...

261
00:15:46.360 --> 00:15:48.460
Crap. Four of us can't swim.

262
00:15:58.440 --> 00:15:59.640
Come on.

263
00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:02.210
Reach!

264
00:16:05.050 --> 00:16:06.680
Nami!

265
00:16:06.680 --> 00:16:08.320
Robin!

266
00:16:10.520 --> 00:16:11.790
Dammit.

267
00:16:11.790 --> 00:16:14.320
I can't resist the current!

268
00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:32.380
That's one way to get in.
Pretty reckless, though.

269
00:16:32.780 --> 00:16:35.780
Well, we can still go in after
them if you want to, Hammond.

270
00:16:35.780 --> 00:16:38.410
No way to know if they're
alive or dead though.

271
00:16:40.150 --> 00:16:41.990
Yeah, let's track them down.

272
00:16:41.990 --> 00:16:45.720
We can't let Neptune's Army get their
hands on them first, now can we?

273
00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:50.490
But before we do anything, we should go
back to Noah and tell the boss what's up.

274
00:16:50.490 --> 00:16:55.000
I think he'd want to know that the man
who ruined Arlong's plan is here.

275
00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:04.240
<b>Fishman Island, on the Seafloor</b>

276
00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:07.110
Hey!

277
00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:11.710
Take a look!

278
00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:12.580
I'll look.

279
00:17:12.580 --> 00:17:13.650
I won't!

280
00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:14.880
Maybe I'll look.

281
00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:16.150
Who cares if I look?

282
00:17:18.860 --> 00:17:20.220
Now he's moving!

283
00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:21.220
He moved!

284
00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:22.730
No, he didn't!

285
00:17:22.730 --> 00:17:24.630
He might've moved.

286
00:17:24.630 --> 00:17:25.960
Who cares if he moved?

287
00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:32.670
All right! He's alive!

288
00:17:32.670 --> 00:17:33.870
Thank goodness!

289
00:17:37.040 --> 00:17:38.470
Oh, Luffy-chin!

290
00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:42.210
It's been a while, hasn't it?

291
00:17:42.210 --> 00:17:44.110
So, how are you feeling?

292
00:17:47.320 --> 00:17:50.850
Hey, it's Camie!
 It's nice to see you!

293
00:17:50.850 --> 00:17:55.460
Oh, Camie, you've gotten so lovely! Marry me!

294
00:17:55.460 --> 00:17:58.290
Then we made it to Fishman Island after all?

295
00:17:58.290 --> 00:17:59.600
Yeah, we did!

296
00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:01.800
From what I understand,
we were about to drown,

297
00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:03.970
but then we were rescued
 by a bunch of mermaids!

298
00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:04.970
That's right!

299
00:18:04.970 --> 00:18:07.870
Sanji, Chopper, and I just
 woke up a few minutes ago.

300
00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:09.110
Guess we're pretty lucky, huh?

301
00:18:09.110 --> 00:18:11.410
Lucky enough to wake up in Camie's house.

302
00:18:11.410 --> 00:18:12.380
Here, catch.

303
00:18:12.380 --> 00:18:14.940
Oh. So, this is your house?

304
00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:16.350
My bad!

305
00:18:16.350 --> 00:18:19.080
I know I was supposed to
 pick you guys up on Sabaody,

306
00:18:19.080 --> 00:18:21.180
but I was thinking that was another month from now.

307
00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:23.450
That's okay!

308
00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:24.520
Where is everybody?

309
00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:26.960
Well, uh...

310
00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:29.360
Looks like we got separated.

311
00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:32.630
Goodness. I hope they're safe.

312
00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:33.860
So, they're lost?

313
00:18:33.860 --> 00:18:37.030
Yeah. Before I blacked out,
 I was trying to follow them,

314
00:18:37.030 --> 00:18:39.640
but that current must've pulled
 them off in a different direction.

315
00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:43.140
Ah, gotcha!
Well, I'm sure it'll turn out okay, right?

316
00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:44.570
They're fine.

317
00:18:44.570 --> 00:18:47.080
The bonehead can't do much underwater,

318
00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:50.580
but the robot and Moss Head
are probably with him. So, I wouldn't worry.

319
00:18:50.950 --> 00:18:53.520
I hope I get to see them again soon.

320
00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:55.080
Anyway, here you go!

321
00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:57.150
I'm sure you're all freezing.

322
00:18:57.150 --> 00:18:59.390
So, I made some soup
that'll warm you right up.

323
00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:01.520
Ta-dah!

324
00:19:01.520 --> 00:19:03.360
Cold seaweed soup!

325
00:19:03.730 --> 00:19:04.460
It's yummy!

326
00:19:08.630 --> 00:19:10.500
It's... cold?

327
00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:11.330
Mm-hm!

328
00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:17.810
That's not right! How are you supposed
to get warm if the soup is cold?

329
00:19:17.810 --> 00:19:19.340
I'm sorry!

330
00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:20.740
Wha...?

331
00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:23.080
I'm such a failure!

332
00:19:25.420 --> 00:19:28.790
But your soup is great, Camie.

333
00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:31.720
I'm warmer already!

334
00:19:31.720 --> 00:19:33.560
That doesn't make sense.

335
00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:35.360
Come on, let me try some, too!

336
00:19:37.890 --> 00:19:39.860
Your clothes are dry, everybody!

337
00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:40.730
They're dry!

338
00:19:40.730 --> 00:19:42.370
No, they're not dry!

339
00:19:42.370 --> 00:19:43.870
Your clothes might be dry.

340
00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:45.130
Who cares if they're dry?

341
00:19:50.970 --> 00:19:52.780
You took care of our clothes, too?

342
00:19:52.780 --> 00:19:53.880
Wow! Thanks!

343
00:19:55.140 --> 00:19:57.410
Who are those little guys?

344
00:19:57.410 --> 00:19:59.350
Oh, they're some friends of mine.

345
00:19:59.350 --> 00:20:01.320
The Medaka Mermaid Quintuplets.

346
00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:02.450
I'm Ichika!

347
00:20:02.450 --> 00:20:03.320
I'm Nika!

348
00:20:03.320 --> 00:20:04.320
I'm Sanka!

349
00:20:04.320 --> 00:20:05.220
I'm Yonka!

350
00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:06.720
And I'm Yonka Two!

351
00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:08.560
Wait, why are there two Yonkas?

352
00:20:09.090 --> 00:20:11.730
They're really fast swimmers,
and pretty clever as well!

353
00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:13.930
Yeah? Nice to meet ya!

354
00:20:13.930 --> 00:20:16.830
I've got a lot of neat friends here, actually.

355
00:20:16.830 --> 00:20:21.100
This is the sea floor of the Mermaid Cove,
home to the girls' dorm of the famous Mermaid Café!

356
00:20:21.400 --> 00:20:23.710
Huh?
The Girls' dorm?

357
00:20:24.070 --> 00:20:25.140
Please, Camie!

358
00:20:25.140 --> 00:20:28.880
Tell me everything about
this Mermaid Café place!

359
00:20:28.880 --> 00:20:32.120
Oh, it's just this cute little café
where I work as a waitress.

360
00:20:32.120 --> 00:20:34.120
We have a lot of pretty
mermaids there on staff.

361
00:20:34.520 --> 00:20:36.250
Ah! Sounds like heaven!

362
00:20:39.060 --> 00:20:41.160
Can I get you anything extra?

363
00:20:44.060 --> 00:20:46.960
– Sanji!
– Don't die!

364
00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:48.800
I won't die!

365
00:20:48.800 --> 00:20:49.770
– False alarm!
– False alarm!

366
00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:52.300
I swore...

367
00:20:52.300 --> 00:20:54.270
I made a promise to myself,

368
00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:57.870
that for the entire time I was on Fishman Island

369
00:20:57.870 --> 00:21:00.440
I wouldn't get a nosebleed and pass out!

370
00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:08.620
And I've held out for this long,
so I deserve a reward, right?

371
00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:10.150
Pathetic.

372
00:21:10.850 --> 00:21:11.450
I know!

373
00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:13.590
Why don't we go up there now?

374
00:21:13.590 --> 00:21:15.530
I'll introduce you to all of my friends!

375
00:21:19.230 --> 00:21:20.400
Whoa! A turtle!

376
00:21:20.900 --> 00:21:23.270
"Sea Turtle Elevator," huh?

377
00:21:25.130 --> 00:21:26.940
Could you give us a lift, Mr. Turtle?

378
00:21:32.580 --> 00:21:35.140
This is a coral apartment complex.

379
00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:38.110
The dorms are at the very
bottom, so rent's cheap.

380
00:21:38.110 --> 00:21:41.650
The top floor's the most expensive
because it gets natural light.

381
00:21:42.550 --> 00:21:44.550
Does that mean you're poor?

382
00:21:44.550 --> 00:21:46.460
And what about Hachi and Pappagu?

383
00:21:46.460 --> 00:21:49.330
Hatchin got beat up real bad about a year ago.

384
00:21:49.330 --> 00:21:51.240
Oh, yeah, I heard about that.

385
00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:54.130
He was protecting the Sunny for us
back on Sabaody, right?

386
00:21:54.130 --> 00:21:57.770
Hatchin came from the Fishman District, so
that's where he's been resting and recovering.

387
00:21:57.770 --> 00:22:01.770
I haven't had the chance to see him lately,
but from what I hear, he's getting better all the time.

388
00:22:02.170 --> 00:22:04.010
Huh? He's okay?

389
00:22:04.660 --> 00:22:06.810
Yeah. But it's kind of a rough part of town.

390
00:22:06.810 --> 00:22:10.450
If you guys go along with me, I wouldn't mind
heading over there to visit him, though.

391
00:22:10.450 --> 00:22:11.610
Let's do it!

392
00:22:11.610 --> 00:22:13.780
I've been wanting to thank him face-to-face.

393
00:22:13.780 --> 00:22:15.590
Sure, you got it!

394
00:22:15.590 --> 00:22:18.320
And, well, as for Pappagu...

395
00:22:19.460 --> 00:22:21.920
He's a super-famous fashion designer.

396
00:22:21.920 --> 00:22:27.530
So, he lives in a big fancy mansion
in the high-class district of Fishverly Hills!

397
00:22:27.530 --> 00:22:31.030
I'm supposed to deliver some clams over
there today. You wanna come with me?

398
00:22:31.370 --> 00:22:33.300
Wait, he's your pet.

399
00:22:33.300 --> 00:22:35.200
But you two don't live in the same place?

400
00:22:36.440 --> 00:22:39.540
Yeah, 'cause that area's
a little out of my price range.

401
00:22:40.010 --> 00:22:42.350
We have better clams here, anyway.

402
00:22:42.880 --> 00:22:44.850
We're almost to the top!

403
00:22:44.860 --> 00:22:48.780
Huh? Hey, what's that
drinking-straw-looking tube dealie?

404
00:22:48.780 --> 00:22:49.990
Oh. That thing?

405
00:22:50.790 --> 00:22:53.590
That's the Water Road.
The bubble craftsmen built it.

406
00:22:53.590 --> 00:22:57.030
And when mermaids or 
fish get inside it... Well, hold on.

407
00:22:57.590 --> 00:22:59.460
Here, let me show you!

408
00:23:05.330 --> 00:23:08.270
It's the surface! We made it!

409
00:23:08.270 --> 00:23:10.670
Luffy-chin!

410
00:23:12.840 --> 00:23:13.540
Look!

411
00:23:13.940 --> 00:23:15.880
I'm swimming in the sky!

412
00:23:15.880 --> 00:23:17.880
– Oh, wow!
– I wanna do that!

413
00:23:19.080 --> 00:23:20.480
Wait a sec!

414
00:23:20.480 --> 00:23:23.920
If we're underwater,
why do I see a sky full of clouds?

415
00:23:24.290 --> 00:23:26.090
Hey! Camie!

416
00:23:26.090 --> 00:23:27.960
Huh? It's a girl!

417
00:23:28.660 --> 00:23:30.590
Hey, guys!

418
00:23:32.560 --> 00:23:36.570
Are these your pirate friends?
I guess that means they didn't drown after all!

419
00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:42.670
You didn't come in through the entrance like
you're supposed to, so we were concerned.

420
00:23:45.210 --> 00:23:46.440
Well, hi there.

421
00:23:46.440 --> 00:23:48.440
You're not as scary as I thought you'd be.

422
00:23:48.440 --> 00:23:49.950
So, you broke in?

423
00:23:49.950 --> 00:23:51.080
That's pretty hot.

424
00:23:51.080 --> 00:23:52.720
I kinda have a thing for pirates.

425
00:24:02.830 --> 00:24:05.290
It's like a real-life fairy tale!

426
00:24:05.290 --> 00:24:09.530
A coral paradise!
A whole cove full of mermaids!

427
00:24:24.380 --> 00:24:26.420
What's the matter with Sanji now?!

428
00:24:26.420 --> 00:24:29.490
He didn't even cry this hard
when he left the Baratie.

429
00:24:32.390 --> 00:24:34.890
Finally!

430
00:24:35.260 --> 00:24:38.630
I found my All Blue after all these years!

431
00:24:40.860 --> 00:24:43.370
Are you sure about that? Really?

432
00:24:44.700 --> 00:24:46.540
Here, let me introduce everybody!

433
00:24:47.040 --> 00:24:49.540
That's Luffy-chin. He's the captain!

434
00:24:49.540 --> 00:24:50.740
Yeah, nice to meet ya!

435
00:24:51.370 --> 00:24:53.210
Sanji-chin's the crybaby.

436
00:24:53.610 --> 00:24:55.710
The nose guy is Usopp-chin!

437
00:24:55.710 --> 00:24:56.450
That's me!

438
00:24:56.950 --> 00:24:59.120
And the raccoon is Chopper-chin!

439
00:24:59.120 --> 00:25:00.220
Not again!

440
00:25:01.420 --> 00:25:04.090
Aw, why are you crying?

441
00:25:05.320 --> 00:25:06.690
Come over here.

442
00:25:06.690 --> 00:25:08.790
Let's dance in the water together!

443
00:25:13.760 --> 00:25:16.400
Okay. I get it.

444
00:25:16.400 --> 00:25:19.000
This is obviously too good to be true.

445
00:25:19.000 --> 00:25:21.800
Maybe... I'm destined to die today.

446
00:25:21.800 --> 00:25:23.270
That's dark!

447
00:25:23.270 --> 00:25:26.780
What the heck happened to you in the
 last two years to make you this gloomy?

448
00:25:26.780 --> 00:25:30.150
Isn't this supposed to be
the land of your dreams?

449
00:25:31.610 --> 00:25:34.020
You crack me up, Sanji!

450
00:25:34.020 --> 00:25:35.720
– I don't think he's joking!
– I don't think he's joking!

451
00:25:43.830 --> 00:25:46.100
Interesting...

452
00:25:45.290 --> 00:25:50.530
<b>Noah, Fishman District</b>

453
00:25:46.100 --> 00:25:50.530
So, Straw Hat finally made it to our turf,
did he? Good for him.

454
00:25:51.600 --> 00:25:52.600
Right!

455
00:25:52.600 --> 00:25:56.570
Wh-What are we gonna do about it, Boss?

456
00:25:58.770 --> 00:26:00.410
I want you to bring him here...

457
00:26:01.780 --> 00:26:03.110
and quickly.
